  "proved_in_this_revision": [
    "PB(E) assembled from internally printed characterwise descent, cyclotomic derivatives, Frobenius selection and Bernoulli integer product",
    "Uniform 24-generator bound for the unramified dyadic module and its split quotient; explicit bidual identifications with Tower.XX and Tower.XP, hence the generator input Tower.IsTower",
    "Full finite-twist cokernel identification by continuous cocycles, and restriction to the canonical CM field with kernel length at most one; uniform finite-twist estimates now proved outside a fixed exceptional set",
    "Centered prime-distribution identity with all half-line boundary terms",
    "Global zeta zero growth bound and uniqueness of a vertical discrete spectral distribution",
    "Counterexample to arbitrary Mellin-transform O(log T) unit-box zero counts and the decreasing-kernel projection check",
    "Rational trivial-character vanishing at 3 and 7 for every positive twist and at every resonant prime ell-1 dividing 2a; elementary quadratic class-number and cyclotomic descent proofs",
    "Full plus-height assembly from two stated rational-character estimates with exponent A+3B+5, and exceptional-pair exponent 2B+2; both input estimates remain unproved here",
    "Absorption of the weaker cubic-logarithmic height envelope in the same windows",
    "Uniform dyadic free-lift congruence A^128 = 1 modulo 8 and cokernel growth c_m(a) <= c_7(a)+24(m-7)_+",
    "Matrix-logarithm center bound with at most 24 fixed centers and exceptional twists on a whole horizon",
    "Fixed-layer discriminant |disc L_7| <= 2^8192 (qd)^512",
    "Full dyadic common-window estimate conditional on specialized high-twist cohomology bound K_2(C_K), which remains unproved",
    "Exact local/global cyclotomic images and H² length s_2(L_m,a)+m+2+v_2(a) in the principal dyadic tower; cohomology growth at most 25(m-7)_+",
    "Fixed Q(sqrt(-3)) auxiliary arithmetic packet for every odd nonresonant prime, including seven; substantial PropGK producer still required",
    "Determinant-prescribed fractional-ideal lattice comparison (SStein), with CRT construction, valuation equivalence and exact Minkowski covolume scaling",
    "Uniform global high-twist cohomology bound, including at 2, with exponent 24, via published K-theory and Hurewicz comparisons plus a full integral torsion and geometric orbit calculation",
    "K_2(24), hence the dyadic common-window bound with C_K=24, eta=epsilon/48 and J=2^26*(19248/epsilon)^24",
    "Bounded-order twist-one polynomial character bound at 3 and 7 with B_R=(6R+1)*(12R)^24",
    "Coefficient-uniform complex cohomology of arithmetic groups, finite adelic orbit count and polynomial congruence-level bound, with the lattice and module arguments printed"
  ],
